# Fleet choices about the mission itself, and the approach mystery thread.
# Arc and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.

card dec_halfway
type decision
cat mission
days 24 25
weight 40
once
duration 1
roles A B
lean warm feast quiet
text Halfway, by the flight plan's clock. {A} wants to break out the good rations and mark it properly. {B} would rather not count yet.
option feast | Mark it | The fleet eats the good rations on seven screens at once. {A} gives a toast about the halfway mark, and it turns into a toast about the people who packed the food.
  res food -2
  morale A 4
  morale B 2
option quiet | Let it pass | Halfway passes without a word on the fleet channel. On every ship, at the same minute, someone looks at the clock anyway.
  bond A B 3

card dec_name
type decision
cat mission
days 26 34
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious after home
text The backup-site maps, stitched from imagery older than the cargo landings (the only sharp camera at Mars rode on the grey relay), show an unnamed crater small enough for the fleet to name. {A} wants to name it after the first person who ever wrote a Mars mission plan. {B} wants somewhere at home.
option after | Honor the planners | The name goes in the request. Somewhere, a committee will argue about it for years, which {A} considers part of the honor.
  set name_plan
  trait A curious 2
option home | Name it for home | The crater gets the name of a small town on Earth that most of Earth has never heard of. Within a day, the town's newspaper has a front page about it.
  set name_home
  trait B warm 3
  morale B 4

card dec_science
type decision
cat mission
days 14 24
weight 8
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious record save
text A gamma-ray burst goes off far past the galaxy, and every ship's X-ray monitor catches it. Timed against detectors near Earth, the raw buffers could pin the source, but pulling them home bumps a day of mail. {A} wants the data sent. {B} wants the letters.
option record | Send the data | The burst's source shrinks from a smear of sky to a thin arc, and the arc runs through one faint galaxy. {A} saves the confirmation in the photo folder.
  morale B -2
  trait A curious 3
  morale A 3
option save | Letters first | Ground telescopes get the burst anyway, less sharply. {B} reads every letter, and doesn't pretend it was an easy trade.
  trait B warm 2

# --- The mystery chain (fixed days; one beat a day from 35 to 41) ------------------
card m_ripple
type event
cat mystery
clue
days 14 14
weight 14
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} cleans up the receiver's noise floor for the weekly report and finds a faint ripple in it, at about nine hundredths of a hertz. A control loop hunting somewhere, most likely the coolant pump's: it's on the same bus. {A} notes it in the margin and moves on to the propellant tables.

card m_dropout
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 24 27
roles A
when since t_theory >= 2
text {A} plots a week of the old-channel carrier for the anomaly file. It isn't steady: there for part of each day, gone for the rest, and back thirty-seven minutes later each morning. {A} blames the dish's scan schedule and moves on to the dust forecast.
do mark t_dropout

card m_theory
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 17 18
roles A
when since t_carrier >= 2
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} looks up the grey relay. Its thruster stuck open just before the cargo landings; three power-only passes afterwards, on a spare antenna, caught it spinning every 10.96 seconds, beam on Earth 2.4 percent of a turn. Nothing else used the channel. {A} sketches a lighthouse in blue.
do who ow_theory A
do mark t_theory
do morale A 3

card m_theory_confirm
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 25 27
roles A
when since t_theory >= 3
when is A ow_theory
text The ground can't run the grey relay forward: its orbit data is two years stale. "Check the dish schedule at your end," the ground says. {A} tapes the lighthouse sketch above the console.
do morale A 2

card c_theory
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text {A} looks at the lighthouse again. A relay would swing the knocks early and late every couple of hours. These swing by a hundredth of a second once a day, and the day is thirty-seven minutes too long. Under the lighthouse, in blue, {A} draws a question mark.
do trait A curious 2

card m_flash1
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 30 31
roles A
when !is A ow_theory
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} pulls an old survey orbiter's low-light night frames of the landing region. On dark ground near the edge of one frame, one pixel is lit. On the next frame it isn't. A cosmic-ray hit on the sensor, almost certainly. {A} logs it with the other sensor hits.
do set flash_seen
do mark t_flash
do who flash_who A
do trait A curious 2

card m_flash2
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 32 33
roles A
when flag flash_seen
when since t_flash >= 2
when is A flash_who
text {A} goes through every night frame of that patch this month. Every pass, on different rows of the sensor, the lit pixel lands on the same spot of ground. {A} sends the list round, asking to be told it's wrong. The ground's first guess: the hopper, tipped on its pad, beacon still coming and going.
do set flash_twice
do open dec_flash

card dec_flash
type decision
cat mystery
days 32 33
weight 1
once
duration 1
roles A B
when flag flash_twice
lean curious look leave
text {A} wants to ask the ground to task an orbiter for a fast sequence over the lit pixel, at the cost of the fleet's next deep-space pass, because the orbiter's data needs the same ground antenna: every letter from home waits. {B} would leave it for the people who'll be down there with time to look.
option look | Ask for the sequence | The request goes up. {A} writes the apology to six inboxes personally, and means each one.
  set flash_looked
  morale A -2
  morale B -2
option leave | Leave it for the ground | The pixel goes into the anomaly file, under a heading {B} writes in capitals. The letters from home arrive on time, all of them.
  set flash_left
  morale B 2

card m_key
type event
cat mystery
clue core key
due
once
days 34 34
roles A
text The ground decodes a whole frame from Mars for {A}: a link request on an old program key, sequence 5,750,112, with a fresh challenge. {A} does the sum: two years, at least. The ground: "Old key. The first batch was re-keyed after landing; only the relay kept it. Nothing on it still flies."
do trait A curious 2

card flash_answer
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_looked
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text The fast sequence comes down overnight: forty frames of dark ground as the orbiter slides over. The pixel lights, goes out, lights again, and never moves against the rocks. {A} counts the frames between flashes, gets the same number each time, and calls the fleet.
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 4

card flash_answer_ground
type event
cat mystery
clue core ground
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when flag flash_left
when since t_flash >= 5
when is A flash_who
text An email from the orbiter team reaches {A}: a calibration slot was free, and the pixel was in the swath. Forty frames of dark ground, the pixel lighting, going out, lighting again, never moving against the rocks. The email ends: "Officially, a star calibration."
do set flash_ground
do trait A curious 3

card c2_cold
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when is A flash_who
when !fired h_band
text The night frames of the pixel have gaps now, longest in the hour before dawn, the coldest there. Each night a gap runs a few knocks longer, and it comes back on the beat. {A} plots the gaps against the calendar: at this rate they meet in the middle a few nights after the fleet lands.
do morale A -2

card m_overlay
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when flag flash_ground
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A flash_who
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} borrows the old-channel receiver record, slides it back by the one-way light time from Mars, about fifteen seconds, and lays it over the forty frames. The carrier peaks on the exact frame the pixel lights. Every time. {A} puts both traces on the galley screen, side by side.
do trait A curious 3

card m_checked
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_looked
text The ground answers the overlay: nothing near that pixel has power. The hopper is ninety kilometres south, its beacon as patchy as ever. Nearest is a scar a few kilometres off, filed two years ago as impact debris. Two weeks of hails on the old key, unanswered. On the list it goes.
do morale A 1

card m_checked_g
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when flag flash_left
text The ground answers the overlay: nothing near that pixel has power. The hopper is ninety kilometres south, its beacon as patchy as ever. Nearest is a scar a few kilometres off, filed two years ago as impact debris. Two weeks of hails on the old key, unanswered. "Surveying it."
do morale A 1

card m_listen
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when fired m_overlay
when is A ow_song
text With Mars a few pages out, the old-channel carrier stands out in a narrow filter, unfolded. {A} turns each burst into a click on the cabin speaker: a click, a hiss, a long pause, a click. The four bars fit between them. {A} plays them on the galley keyboard, stopping where the fifth should be.
do morale A -1

card a_drill_plan
type beat
cat mission
due
once
days 31 33
roles A
when cond A ok
text The surface team sends the landing-site plan, and {A} reads it out. Water first: Cargo 3's ice drill made it down with one bit, rated for a season. The engineer who built it adds a line at the bottom: "Be gentle with it."
do trait A curious 1

card m_count
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when !is A ow_theory
when !is A ow_hail
text {A} times the old-channel carrier on the galley clock, like lightning to thunder. Ten, eleven, knock. The fleet's round trip to the planet is twenty-odd seconds now, and shrinking. {A} writes both on the whiteboard, one above the other.

# --- The payoff: fires on day 40 in every season ------------------------------------
card m_reveal
type event
cat mystery
reveal
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text The fleet's long lenses make the first sharp pass over the backup site in two years: behind a crater rim, a ship stands on its legs, tilted, one solar wing half open, dish jammed against its stop, talking on its low-gain antenna: Cargo 2. With each knock its pad strobe flares, the pad crew's sign it's awake, then goes dark while it listens. {A} counts the dark: nine, ten, eleven, flare.
do trait A curious 3

card a_report
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 40 40
roles A
when fired m_reveal
when is A flash_who
text {A} reads out the board's finding. Boulders on the site: Cargo 2 hovered, diverted behind the rim and set down whole. Its last patch, tested only at Starbase, files any touchdown on a surveyed site as a pad, and the backup site was surveyed. On a pad it obeys the pad crew, not the ground: knock, listen one tick for a signed hello, knock again. Earth's answer takes sixteen minutes. The tick is eleven seconds.

# --- Day 41: the window, one card per carrier branch --------------------------------
card a_window_hail
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10:07: Cargo 2 knocks. {A}'s receiver hears it five seconds later and answers at once, signed. Entry week is frozen, but this hello has been on the schedule, cleared, since the vote: the ground lets it finish the handshake and nothing more, and Cargo 2 stays in its safe hold. It lands a breath before the next tick. By the next night pass the strobe is off; one status lamp burns steady.
do set c2_answered
do morale A 8

card a_log
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when fired a_window_hail
when !is A ow_hail
text Then Cargo 2 sends its event-recorder summary down the old channel. HAIL RX · WRONG CHALLENGE ×31,000: five weeks of Earth's hails. HELLO RX · LATE · DISCARD ×41,000: the fleet's, about twenty ticks late at first, one at the last. At the bottom, one new line: HELLO RX · OK. {A} reads it twice and files it.
do morale A 2

card a_window_quiet
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text 04:10:07: Cargo 2 knocks. Ten seconds there and back now, inside the tick, and nothing on the schedule answers it. The ground drafted a reply the day the key decoded; it reached the board a day into entry week, and the board won't wake a ship that has rebooted itself for two years while seven others steer by it, or circle over it. Until every ship is down: a suit beside it, or nothing.
do morale A -2

# --- Day 41: the descent brief, one per arrival branch ----------------------------
card a_descent_hold
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text The descent brief goes up, and the formation opens out to two minutes between ships. The storm fills the prime zone rim to rim. The backup site is no clearer, but it is flat, it was surveyed, and now it has a landmark that answers. The brief gains a line no one has written before: "radar for height, Cargo 2's radio for place". {A} flies the manual takeover once in the sim, from memory.
do morale A 2

card a_descent_hold_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when !flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text The descent brief goes up, and the formation opens out to two minutes between ships. The storm fills the prime zone rim to rim. The backup site is no clearer, but it is flat, it was surveyed, and now it has a landmark that knocks every eleven seconds. New line: "radar for height, last orbiter fix for place, Cargo 2's knock to cross-check". {A} flies the manual takeover once in the sim, from memory.

card a_descent_wait
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when !is A ow_hail
when !flag c2_answered
text In four days the fleet dips into the upper atmosphere instead of landing through it, into the long orbit, to wait. Below, the storm lies over the landing zone like a hand over a mouth. {A} finds the light on the night frames, fainter in the dust, still keeping time, and sits down with the ration tables. The entry team clears every heat-shield tile again, this time for two trips through the air.
do morale A -2

card a_descent_wait_a
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
text In four days the fleet dips into the upper atmosphere instead of landing through it, into the long orbit, to wait. Below, the storm lies over the landing zone like a hand over a mouth. {A} finds the light on the night frames, fainter in the dust, steady now, and sits down with the ration tables. The entry team clears every heat-shield tile again, this time for two trips through the air.
do morale A -1

card a_descent_clear
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag arrive_hold
when !flag arrive_wait
when is A ow_hail
text The descent brief goes up four days out: clear air, straight in, the formation opening out to two minutes between ships. The prime zone is exactly where the maps said, with one more thing thirty kilometres past it. {A} packs a bag for the drive out: water, a torch, spare batteries, a marker.
do morale A 3
